[
    {
        "id": "hal_tab",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "Halloween Show",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "What Halloween does when the show is switched.\n\nListens to house/show/command (retained on/off from the Holiday Shows tab when Holiday Season = Halloween, or from switch.halloween_eyes_show). The demoneye Pis follow the same topic on their own (eyes + projectors).\n\nGovee: on -> blue fire, off -> night mode. The first message after a deploy or restart (the retained one) is ignored.\n\n'eyes command' is a spare publisher to house/show/command (not wired)."
    },
    {
        "id": "lights_comment",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "hal_tab",
        "name": "Govee lights follow the show",
        "info": "Listens to the same retained command the Pis use, so the lights change whether the show is switched by the schedule above or by hand from switch.halloween_eyes_show.\n\nOn  -> scene.govee_to_mqtt_one_click_leisure_blue_fire\nOff -> scene.govee_to_mqtt_one_click_leisure_night_mode\n\nBoth are Govee Tap-to-Runs synced into HA by govee2mqtt. To use different scene names, edit the two action nodes.\n\nThe filter ignores the first message after a deploy or restart (the retained one), so redeploying Node-RED at noon won't turn the lights on.",
        "x": 200,
        "y": 60,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "7edf248943d6c9c3",
        "type": "mqtt in",
        "z": "hal_tab",
        "name": "show command",
        "topic": "house/show/command",
        "qos": "1",
        "datatype": "utf8",
        "broker": "eyes_broker",
        "nl": false,
        "rap": true,
        "rh": 0,
        "inputs": 0,
        "x": 160,
        "y": 120,
        "wires": [
            [
                "809a6005569f758d"
            ]
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "809a6005569f758d",
        "type": "function",
        "z": "hal_tab",
        "name": "on / off",
        "func": "// Same rules as the eyes (directors.py _parse_command), so the lights can\n// never disagree with the Pis about whether the show is on.\nconst ON = [\"on\", \"1\", \"true\", \"play\", \"start\", \"yes\", \"open\"];\nconst OFF = [\"off\", \"0\", \"false\", \"stop\", \"pause\", \"no\", \"close\"];\n\nlet v = msg.payload;\nif (Buffer.isBuffer(v)) v = v.toString();\nif (v !== null && typeof v === \"object\") {\n    v = v.state ?? \"\";\n} else {\n    v = String(v ?? \"\").trim().replace(/^\"|\"$/g, \"\");\n    if (v.startsWith(\"{\")) {\n        try { v = JSON.parse(v).state ?? \"\"; } catch (e) { return null; }\n    }\n}\nv = String(v).trim().toLowerCase();\n\nif (ON.includes(v)) msg.payload = \"on\";\nelse if (OFF.includes(v)) msg.payload = \"off\";\nelse return null;\nreturn msg;",
        "outputs": 1,
        "timeout": 0,
        "noerr": 0,
        "initialize": "",
        "finalize": "",
        "libs": [],
        "x": 340,
        "y": 120,
        "wires": [
            [
                "2fcbbcd822032018"
            ]
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "2fcbbcd822032018",
        "type": "rbe",
        "z": "hal_tab",
        "name": "only on change",
        "func": "rbei",
        "gap": "",
        "start": "",
        "inout": "out",
        "septopics": false,
        "property": "payload",
        "topi": "topic",
        "x": 510,
        "y": 120,
        "wires": [
            [
                "63f5f2d388e887f2"
            ]
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "63f5f2d388e887f2",
        "type": "switch",
        "z": "hal_tab",
        "name": "show?",
        "property": "payload",
        "propertyType": "msg",
        "rules": [
            {
                "t": "eq",
                "v": "on",
                "vt": "str"
            },
            {
                "t": "eq",
                "v": "off",
                "vt": "str"
            }
        ],
        "checkall": "false",
        "repair": false,
        "outputs": 2,
        "x": 670,
